[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: An idempotent writer reporting unchanged proves nothing about whether it can write

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-IDEMPOTENT-WRITER-UNCHANGED-IS-NOT-PROOF
TITLE: An idempotent writer reporting unchanged proves nothing about whether it can write
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
generate:sgra skips a file whose bytes already match and logs `unchanged`. So
does a run whose target path is wrong, whose cwd anchor is wrong, or whose
comparison is inverted. Every one of those logs `unchanged` and exits 0, against
a file it never touched, and the reassuring word is the same in all four cases.

The first run of the write task on 2026-08-27 reported exactly that against
docs/sdoc/grammar.sgra. It was believed only after DELETING the file and
re-running, which logged `wrote` and reproduced the committed bytes; that
sequence is what makes the write and the byte-identity claim one measurement
instead of two assertions sitting next to each other.

The shape is not local to this task: dev/tasks/generate.nix's `sync_file` has the
same blind spot, and so does any comparison-first writer. Fix shape, if one is
wanted, is to make the log carry the path that was compared, so a wrong anchor
prints a wrong path rather than a right-sounding word.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Logged because the failure is silent and self-confirming in the direction a
session already wants to believe: a generator that appears to have nothing to do
is indistinguishable from a generator that is already correct.
<<<
